@startuml card-domain-relations
title card.domain — model relations

' Names and relations only. Column-level properties are a later task.
' A solid arrow that leaves this context is an id. Contexts do not share tables.
' A dashed arrow is a dependency of the purchase walk, not a table this context owns.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

package card {
  package domain {
    enum PurchaseStatus {
      REQUESTED
      AUTHORIZED
      CLEARED
      SETTLED
      POSTED
    }

    class Card
    class Purchase
    class AuthorizationHold

    Purchase "*" --> "1" Card : card
    Purchase "*" --> "1" PurchaseStatus : status
    Purchase "1" --> "1" AuthorizationHold : hold
  }
}

package customer <<external>> {
  package domain {
    class Customer
  }
}

package ledger <<external>> {
  package domain {
    class Account
    class JournalEntry
  }
}

Card "1" --> "1" Customer : holder
AuthorizationHold ..> Account : available balance\nvia card → customer → deposit account
Purchase ..> JournalEntry : customer posting\n2100 debit, 2300 credit

note bottom of Card
  Addressed by its public token, not by a raw number.
  Fixture token: card_ada_orquidea.
end note

note bottom of AuthorizationHold
  A reservation against available balance.
  Open from AUTHORIZED until the customer is posted,
  then released in that same transaction.
  Does not write the journal.
  Every persisted Purchase has one hold.
  A decline writes no purchase and no hold.
end note

note bottom of Purchase
  The walk. Status is the debugger's progress marker.
  SETTLED: the customer is posted and the amount sits in suspense.
  POSTED: the merchant has been paid.
  ClearingItem and Settlement live in settlement
  and reference this purchase.
end note

@enduml
